---
number: 127
title: Low in the Grave He Lay
author: Robert Lowry
composer: Robert Lowry
sp_category: "10"
topic: Christ’s Resurrection and Ascension
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
Low in the grave He lay—
Jesus, my Saviour!
Waiting the coming day—
Jesus, my Lord!

[chorus]
Up from the grave He arose
With a mighty triumph o’er His foes;
He arose a Victor from the dark domain,
And He lives forever with His saint to reign;
He arose! He arose!
Hallelujah! Christ arose!

[verse 2]
Vainly they watch His bed—
Jesus, my Saviour!
Vainly they seal the dead—
Jesus, my Lord!

[chorus]
Up from the grave He arose
With a mighty triumph o’er His foes;
He arose a Victor from the dark domain,
And He lives forever with His saint to reign;
He arose! He arose!
Hallelujah! Christ arose!

[verse 3]
Death cannot keep His prey—
Jesus, my Saviour!
He tore the bars away—
Jesus, my Lord!

[chorus]
Up from the grave He arose
With a mighty triumph o’er His foes;
He arose a Victor from the dark domain,
And He lives forever with His saint to reign;
He arose! He arose!
Hallelujah! Christ arose!
